summary: Test Kdump by crashing Kernel using crasher Kernel module.
description: |
    It crashes the system by using crasher Kernel module. It could take an
    argument from 0-3,

     * ACP: invoke dump using panic [ panic test 0 ].
     * ACB: invoke dump using BUG [ panic test 1 ].
     * ACE: invoke dump using panic_on_oops [ panic test 2 ].
     * ACL: invoke dump in a hang situation.

    By default, it uses 0 (ACP).
contact: Kdump QE <kdump-qe-list@redhat.com>
test: make run
framework: shell
require:
  - kernel-devel
  - elfutils-libelf-devel
  - gcc
  - kexec-tools
duration: 1h
extra-summary: /kernel/kdump/crash-crasher
extra-task: /kernel/kdump/crash-crasher

/panic:
  environment:
    TESTARGS: 0

/bug:
  environment:
    TESTARGS: 1

/panic_on_oops:
  environment:
    TESTARGS: 2

/spinlock:
  environment:
    TESTARGS: 3

/bug_spinlock:
  environment:
    TESTARGS: 4

